idea:
Extend experiment 7 (the lowest dev so far, 1.8047) into a three-tier curriculum: fill the budget with new text instead of repeated passes, and read it from least to most target-like, ending on pure tier A.

1. Tier A: the current pipeline's kept set (2000-token-head bigram hit rate, LOO threshold thr, junk filter), with one change. Dedupe by best copy instead of first occurrence: group by the '= title =' key (lowercased, non-letters removed), or else by the 200-char normalised prefix, and keep the highest-scoring copy. Count gpt2 tokens with tiktoken. If A holds at least 1.02*T tokens, cap by score, apply the seeded shuffle and return, as now.

2. Tier B (near-miss wiki articles), as in experiment 7:
   - first line is '= title =' and the title key is not in A;
   - bigram hit rate >= thr - 0.08;
   - fraction of alphabetic tokens in the target vocabulary >= 2nd percentile of the target LOO value - 0.05;
   - at least 50 tokens and clean-character fraction >= 0.85;
   - one doc per title key, the highest-scoring one.
   Take at most 0.35*T tokens, highest score first.

3. Tier C (clean general English prose from other domains, new in this experiment). Candidates are docs not in A or B, after exact and prefix dedupe, that meet all of:
   - bigram hit rate >= 0.6*thr;
   - target-vocabulary fraction >= 2nd percentile of the target LOO value - 0.10;
   - clean-character fraction >= 0.92;
   - at least 100 tokens;
   - fraction of characters in '{}[]<>|=;#_/\\' below 1.5%, which removes code and '|' spam;
   - at least one sentence end ('. ' or ' . ') per 60 tokens;
   - no '= title =' first line, so shuffled wiki copies stay out.
   Sort by bigram hit rate descending. Take at most min(0.25*T, T - tokens(A) - tokens(B)) tokens, and nothing if that is <= 0.

4. Sequence, built explicitly with a total of T to 1.02*T tokens so the trainer never wraps:
   - First: all of C, seeded-shuffled.
   - Middle: B mixed with extra seeded-shuffled passes of A as needed to fill, shuffled together.
   - Last: one full seeded-shuffled pass of A, capped to the highest-scoring 0.6*T tokens.
   No global shuffle afterwards.

5. Print tokens(A)/T, tokens(B)/T, tokens(C)/T, the doc count of each tier and the number of extra A passes. Seed everything from CURATE_SEED and keep runtime under 150 seconds, using len/4 token estimates if tiktoken runs late.
